ted this last season at  the dragon pit and thanks to the mission  beyond the wall it now looks like the  whites can be killed by Valyrian steel  too this was the weapon John was using  when he went to capture the white now  when it comes to the White Walkers which  are created by Craster Suns we have only  seen two different types of weapons kill  them we have seen two different White  Walkers get killed by dragon glass  thanks to Samwell Tarly and mirror Reed  then we saw Jon Snow killed two other  way walkers with his Valyrian steel  sword as of right now it doesn't look  like fire can kill the White Walkers  because we have seen them walk right  through fire on a number of different  occasions we have even seen the night  King walk right through the dragon fire  beyond the wall now Daenerys should be  able to kill most of the whites with our  dragons from the sky but in order to  kill the White Walkers and maybe even  the night king they're gonna have to get  up close and personal in order to do  this that is of course unless they were  able to use up  and arrow now as of right now there are  only a handful of Valyrian steel weapons  left as we all know John Snow has a  Valyrian steel sword called Longclaw  Arya Stark has a Valyrian steel dagger  known as the cat's paw  Brienne of Tarth has a Valyrian steel  sword called Oathkeeper given to her by  Jaime Lannister Samwell Tarly took his  family's ancestral Valyrian steel sword  called hearts Bane although now it looks  like Sir Jerome Mormont maybe he's in  that sword during the battle and of  course since Joffrey and Tommen are both  dead Jaime Lannister now has the  Valyrian steel sword what as well since  these are the characters that have the  Valyrian steel weapons we will most  likely see them go up against most of  the White Walkers the faster you can  take out the White Walkers the faster  you can take out all the whites last  season we found out that every time you  kill a white Walker you can also kill  all of the White's he was commanding  that's a very valuable piece of  information if they can somehow get to  the White Walkers are the night king  fast enough then we can start to see  very large groups of whites die  simultaneously the only problem is this  will not be an easy task the episode is  expected to be the longest consecutive  battle sequence ever committed to film  and brings the largest number of major  characters together since the show's  debut this final face-off between the  army of the Dead and the army of the  living is completely unprecedented and  relentless in a mixture of genres even  within the battle there are said to be  sequences built within sequences built  within sequences now the one thing about  this battle that will be very  interesting is the way we get to see it  unfold if you remember the Battle of the  bastards we saw most of the battle  through the eyes of Jon Snow  that was the character we followed  throughout the battle but that will not  be the case for the battle in Winterfell  since there are so many major characters  fighting at the same time the camera  will move around from character to  character during some of the most  intense moments of the battle this will  actually be the very first time we have  seen Arya Stark fight in a battle which  is kind of crazy because we have seen  her training the most the director of  the episode Miguel Sabatini called  Maisie Williams a year before the  filming even begun he told her to start  training for her scenes immediately  because what she will be doing is very  difficult we even got a small taste of  this in the new  trailer it sounds like arias star will  be kicking some major ass during the  battle now it says when the director was  getting ready to start filming the  episode he tried to find a longer battle  sequence in cinema history but it says  he couldn't the closest thing that he  could find was the nearly 40-minute  helms deep sea Jin the Lord of the Rings  which 